## 3. What happens when it goes wrong

<!-- TODO: what is expected of whoever tried, what is expected of the team, and what will NOT
     happen. -->

**The clause that decides whether this is real: the marker stays.**

The `Asistido-por-IA` trailer on a pull request that went badly is **not removed, not omitted, and
not up for discussion**. It is the only way the permission means anything: if the marker disappears
from the failed attempts, the record measures **successes only**, and this team will have learned
exactly what this file exists to prevent.

> **And it is checkable.** Compare the marker rate on reverted or hotfixed pull requests against
> the overall rate. If they differ, the agreement is written and not being kept — which is rather
> more useful than the number alone.

